{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "voices": [
    "en-US-AndrewNeural"
  ],
  "rate": "-3%",
  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "10",
      "part": "17",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m10p17-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "597b803b89f1bccc7044e34b0b71a72bbe08e0aac5d1c526966ade52f0f510bb",
        "2": "986afb6bac34b6c49348362d0aef1ef9963a0b8ed1162d40415ff12a182653ff"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m10p17-andrew-exp-s01-c1-b5cb573bec41",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "An E F S job is fine all morning, then demand spikes. In Bursting mode, Standard-class storage sets the baseline. When metered use stays below it, the unused headroom earns credits for a later spike.",
          "text_sha256": "b5cb573bec41cef6e42c17583404f7ef9debbabc71078cb31c688e27fc2f09ad",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f9f7e73cf5410bcaa3e93a369b5dc84adab9866706479993350db5dd21d7a88e",
          "asset_sha256": "597b803b89f1bccc7044e34b0b71a72bbe08e0aac5d1c526966ade52f0f510bb"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p17-andrew-exp-s01-c2-938e4bf4426d",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Now the job needs more than the baseline. It can draw from the credit balance within its burst limits. A healthy balance buys it time, not a permanently higher rate.",
          "text_sha256": "938e4bf4426d2624430036d896a124e08dc57f295434a2bc9fb01d3a1fd67e34",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "938e4bf4426d2624430036d896a124e08dc57f295434a2bc9fb01d3a1fd67e34",
          "asset_sha256": "597b803b89f1bccc7044e34b0b71a72bbe08e0aac5d1c526966ade52f0f510bb"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p17-andrew-exp-s01-c3-a7f72b7dcad2",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "What happens if the peak keeps going? When credits run out, sustained throughput follows the baseline and applicable limits. Compare the balance with the periods when the job slows.",
          "text_sha256": "a7f72b7dcad27802e2099607ca98eddb2570141aebc33216f7d9ba8c24af1c50",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a7f72b7dcad27802e2099607ca98eddb2570141aebc33216f7d9ba8c24af1c50",
          "asset_sha256": "597b803b89f1bccc7044e34b0b71a72bbe08e0aac5d1c526966ade52f0f510bb"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p17-andrew-exp-s01-c4-66b8ca34a540",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Reads and writes are metered differently. If this workload regularly exceeds the baseline, choose a throughput mode that matches sustained demand rather than relying on the credits to refill during the peak.",
          "text_sha256": "66b8ca34a54008e1b1838a439fd8324b1c460fd3912ca29660bc59e2726c999a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "66b8ca34a54008e1b1838a439fd8324b1c460fd3912ca29660bc59e2726c999a",
          "asset_sha256": "597b803b89f1bccc7044e34b0b71a72bbe08e0aac5d1c526966ade52f0f510bb"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p17-andrew-exp-s02-c1-cea947b74d79",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Replication first copies the existing E F S data, then sends changes asynchronously. A replica can exist without holding the latest write. The first sync takes time and depends on the dataset.",
          "text_sha256": "cea947b74d79bcd47c8f8b219d7dd346a5fef16260cccae111dbb6957f832949",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "04897cf338bbfabdc0ae480818e34033115fc626a36e70335a064129153ab5e6",
          "asset_sha256": "986afb6bac34b6c49348362d0aef1ef9963a0b8ed1162d40415ff12a182653ff"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p17-andrew-exp-s02-c2-cc6733bd4659",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Check Time Since Last Sync and verify the latest usable records. A W S documents a fifteen-minute recovery-point objective for most file systems once the initial sync finishes, with exceptions. That is about potential data loss, not when the app will be back.",
          "text_sha256": "cc6733bd46592f6a76b7e7538667241afeb6db003fa1b1a261f4fc0cfa998829",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "49a9aa927f54da088c7daa62eb06cd69e126711da7f04183adabb0466663d519",
          "asset_sha256": "986afb6bac34b6c49348362d0aef1ef9963a0b8ed1162d40415ff12a182653ff"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p17-andrew-exp-s02-c3-2b00db2d76e1",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "When you fail over, use the intended replication procedure to make the destination writable. Do not send the application to a read-only replica and count the switch as recovered.",
          "text_sha256": "2b00db2d76e15ffa063b28ec42441c3885c6cad2cf414818c8bf5751421ecebf",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2b00db2d76e15ffa063b28ec42441c3885c6cad2cf414818c8bf5751421ecebf",
          "asset_sha256": "986afb6bac34b6c49348362d0aef1ef9963a0b8ed1162d40415ff12a182653ff"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p17-andrew-exp-s02-c4-bd40f6caceaf",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Check mount targets, name resolution, I A M and any required key access. Then try an application read and write. Measure recovery time through that successful test.",
          "text_sha256": "bd40f6caceafdf8f5a75687c2dae44a4a45cbf69ff8fa37a28458d510cbc134e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5d931d1b070729f3de743b1e4fd2f23f4fa724e5a1d0340172573ba4964a8e0b",
          "asset_sha256": "986afb6bac34b6c49348362d0aef1ef9963a0b8ed1162d40415ff12a182653ff"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "10",
      "part": "18",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m10p18-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "050674a4fb9eb2f51ef36beed24d6a1a3b9c2e9f6e4485e6390fc486415d19ba",
        "2": "dd142883dfb84ef27729892b8ba04f5573bde0931feb83ea219adbf706c9b9ce",
        "3": "b9aab5b05bec87367e5102493ee51a484bb48e55c3d906a551f9df2858c7011c",
        "4": "ebb09d3f4dc112d8319dcfc9b036a78a0150ed5361e5136107b724fefc3a171f"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m10p18-andrew-exp-s01-c1-4394f3a2a84e",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "The file closes on the local share. Can the cloud processor start now? Not from that signal alone. The gateway uploads to S three asynchronously, so first establish that the object arrived.",
          "text_sha256": "4394f3a2a84e6da42a10241cc77a2dbf1ca34dea8b4d9853d7f5ff058ffdcb5a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ba5b4354d53ec62bea8d6008b267d79e2be82fee0c9aa55f57e6585d0c4c67a7",
          "asset_sha256": "050674a4fb9eb2f51ef36beed24d6a1a3b9c2e9f6e4485e6390fc486415d19ba"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p18-andrew-exp-s01-c2-a3279e30e9ea",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Use the completed S three object event or an appropriate gateway upload notification. Lambda can process that input into a separate output location, then Athena or Redshift Spectrum can query supported output. Filter the trigger so the output doesn't start the same job again.",
          "text_sha256": "a3279e30e9eac1e7466050648a61d501d769fd579facae19eabc4b79c97bd7f6",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d2368ae2000974a2cd741d3fe7c468c63d018f0b9a39dd60cd10a64f9160cbec",
          "asset_sha256": "050674a4fb9eb2f51ef36beed24d6a1a3b9c2e9f6e4485e6390fc486415d19ba"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p18-andrew-exp-s01-c3-19d1f059876d",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "If the data needs a disaster recovery copy, configure replication with versioning and permissions. It does not make the local write synchronous or coordinate two gateways editing the same file.",
          "text_sha256": "19d1f059876d90f30a5903be249cf1061e90f0186826bff2945fde52f5a4807c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "19d1f059876d90f30a5903be249cf1061e90f0186826bff2945fde52f5a4807c",
          "asset_sha256": "050674a4fb9eb2f51ef36beed24d6a1a3b9c2e9f6e4485e6390fc486415d19ba"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p18-andrew-exp-s02-c1-c496c19581a4",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Site A writes objects to the bucket through its gateway. Pick one writer for this object set; the shared bucket is not a distributed file lock.",
          "text_sha256": "c496c19581a42e999e62bbfcac70ff03814263b89edc78e589d688baa8c83ba2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c496c19581a42e999e62bbfcac70ff03814263b89edc78e589d688baa8c83ba2",
          "asset_sha256": "dd142883dfb84ef27729892b8ba04f5573bde0931feb83ea219adbf706c9b9ce"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p18-andrew-exp-s02-c2-2d5c53677ba1",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Sites B and C read through their own read-only shares. They can see the shared data without giving them another way to overwrite it.",
          "text_sha256": "2d5c53677ba1ecea4bc2795edd10ccb807626cc2053c88cc1698bce11e78c82a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2d5c53677ba1ecea4bc2795edd10ccb807626cc2053c88cc1698bce11e78c82a",
          "asset_sha256": "dd142883dfb84ef27729892b8ba04f5573bde0931feb83ea219adbf706c9b9ce"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p18-andrew-exp-s02-c3-8c923cac35ea",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "After an external change, Refresh Cache updates the reader's inventory when needed. It does not download everything. Check that the client can open the expected file and read its contents.",
          "text_sha256": "8c923cac35eaeebff76df6cf600fb352e0551e532cf5eed0102ae1dc0ff448ed",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "8c923cac35eaeebff76df6cf600fb352e0551e532cf5eed0102ae1dc0ff448ed",
          "asset_sha256": "dd142883dfb84ef27729892b8ba04f5573bde0931feb83ea219adbf706c9b9ce"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p18-andrew-exp-s03-c1-00fd55c0b776",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "A backup writes through File Gateway. When a later backup replaces that key, versioning preserves the earlier copy, so recovery need not depend on the latest write.",
          "text_sha256": "00fd55c0b776ea20bc8ca1094273bda5c8e916defb1de67f24fc86673a646b12",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "00fd55c0b776ea20bc8ca1094273bda5c8e916defb1de67f24fc86673a646b12",
          "asset_sha256": "b9aab5b05bec87367e5102493ee51a484bb48e55c3d906a551f9df2858c7011c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p18-andrew-exp-s03-c2-e03b793867f1",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Lifecycle can save storage costs by moving eligible versions to colder classes. Check retrieval time and charges before choosing an archive tier for data the client may need quickly.",
          "text_sha256": "e03b793867f1bf5b32768e6ec01fc738c97ecfb5d7d8dfeea5238334aef0fa3f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e03b793867f1bf5b32768e6ec01fc738c97ecfb5d7d8dfeea5238334aef0fa3f",
          "asset_sha256": "b9aab5b05bec87367e5102493ee51a484bb48e55c3d906a551f9df2858c7011c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p18-andrew-exp-s03-c3-a288ee2978ca",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Object Lock can protect a retained version even if the next backup writes a newer version under the same key. Here the version we want is version two.",
          "text_sha256": "a288ee2978caa8efbba4a0d42de5f267f887f4e4cab4f5ef42929c7125bf7184",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a288ee2978caa8efbba4a0d42de5f267f887f4e4cab4f5ef42929c7125bf7184",
          "asset_sha256": "b9aab5b05bec87367e5102493ee51a484bb48e55c3d906a551f9df2858c7011c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p18-andrew-exp-s03-c4-b6e9dd2841f7",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "If version two is in Flexible Retrieval or Deep Archive, restore that exact archived version and wait until it is readable. That alone does not make it current. If version three or a delete marker is current, copy version two as a new current version or to a recovery key under the share, in a readable class. Refresh the gateway inventory and verify the file from the client.",
          "text_sha256": "b6e9dd2841f73180660625117117a715a8180ef23d21fe2f73ffdbbced11eeaa",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b6e9dd2841f73180660625117117a715a8180ef23d21fe2f73ffdbbced11eeaa",
          "asset_sha256": "b9aab5b05bec87367e5102493ee51a484bb48e55c3d906a551f9df2858c7011c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p18-andrew-exp-s04-c1-da768c52127e",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "For a Volume Gateway backup, make an E B S volume from the cloud snapshot and attach it to the E C two workload. Check that the expected data is readable; a listed snapshot is not a recovery test.",
          "text_sha256": "da768c52127e06b7a0ebdcdf864652ade679ec2393baf674b33677797e4851f4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5a66833cc100f1bb273648e21f8df9d8d47f5ca1e844887193c69b187297848a",
          "asset_sha256": "ebb09d3f4dc112d8319dcfc9b036a78a0150ed5361e5136107b724fefc3a171f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p18-andrew-exp-s04-c2-62810fe6b6e5",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Tape Gateway follows a different path. Retrieve the virtual tape to the gateway, then restore the files using compatible backup software. If locally buffered data never uploaded, neither recovery path can bring it back from the cloud.",
          "text_sha256": "62810fe6b6e57bea37517ded0b91b67526b7577dbbebd15f09f11eb061f650df",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "62810fe6b6e57bea37517ded0b91b67526b7577dbbebd15f09f11eb061f650df",
          "asset_sha256": "ebb09d3f4dc112d8319dcfc9b036a78a0150ed5361e5136107b724fefc3a171f"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "10",
      "part": "19",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m10p19-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "3d6455f6ea9a2bd5916540f387cff73b01986771446ba44f4a2b94d3e4854bd5"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m10p19-andrew-exp-s01-c1-14069dad1b6c",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Consider Lustre Intelligent-Tiering when only part of a large parallel dataset stays active. Provision throughput separately. An optional S S D read cache can help the hot working set, but the cache is not the durable copy.",
          "text_sha256": "14069dad1b6c6d87de672ba6cb394ef6bb4fa65854974f4e193e75b2d52ac400",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7b0d6597ef6692644b1493f81a43c2fce8b87da0fe770f7849bd8350a1f2b663",
          "asset_sha256": "3d6455f6ea9a2bd5916540f387cff73b01986771446ba44f4a2b94d3e4854bd5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p19-andrew-exp-s01-c2-f8bc073cf649",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "As data becomes less active, it can move through its built-in tiers. This isn't a Glacier restore workflow. It also doesn't support an S three data repository association; pick a supported configuration if that link is required.",
          "text_sha256": "f8bc073cf649e1aeb47db92020ffa6c21ff3f08062c03230b5e0fb0fab8c36d8",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9ebf621eeed6f025e283b6e218c6ad272f684f5f870ea1417b0f5e7761766c84",
          "asset_sha256": "3d6455f6ea9a2bd5916540f387cff73b01986771446ba44f4a2b94d3e4854bd5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p19-andrew-exp-s01-c3-f532ce6163a8",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Copies across Availability Zones improve data durability. They do not guarantee uninterrupted service to the clients. Test the application path and keep a separate recovery plan.",
          "text_sha256": "f532ce6163a855dff0ffe1e97bcc409343d921e03495843bd68024674fa0f557",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f532ce6163a855dff0ffe1e97bcc409343d921e03495843bd68024674fa0f557",
          "asset_sha256": "3d6455f6ea9a2bd5916540f387cff73b01986771446ba44f4a2b94d3e4854bd5"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "10",
      "part": "20",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m10p20-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "516826adf50562626a931e89b4bddd0f4dbe682a64d2984ea2f97a1db32b68cf",
        "2": "d1ac2cae61478a703f7766dc721d7977a77dfe0fc527f1ab8f36060457b89873",
        "3": "34258d0c96e8494227fa11b57fe718f137748caef619356632a1f4b7dc4e758f"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m10p20-andrew-exp-s01-c1-66c99f0813eb",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Start with a disk the E C two instance sees as blocks. E B S can persist apart from the instance, and a volume can be detached and attached again within its zone. The operating system still makes a filesystem or database use those blocks.",
          "text_sha256": "66c99f0813eb218933ca8c96ee5ed5e467cf964e0c9328aa0495c96b19a2b0de",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e1fa01641c5b6ce55fc2a06c64d659234fd3c18de98e69f2a9e2e0a37415e27a",
          "asset_sha256": "516826adf50562626a931e89b4bddd0f4dbe682a64d2984ea2f97a1db32b68cf"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p20-andrew-exp-s01-c2-8a1d2baeedf3",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "If the recovery instance lives in another zone, make a new volume there from a snapshot. That moves a copy of the data, not the original attachment.",
          "text_sha256": "8a1d2baeedf3fd6134c40a3415225e9609dc1d2c0a41f44d869c670be42ea6d6",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "8a1d2baeedf3fd6134c40a3415225e9609dc1d2c0a41f44d869c670be42ea6d6",
          "asset_sha256": "516826adf50562626a931e89b4bddd0f4dbe682a64d2984ea2f97a1db32b68cf"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p20-andrew-exp-s01-c3-03f744012a65",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Choose capacity, I ops and throughput for the workload. E B S is not an N F S or S M B share. Multi-Attach is a specialized case where supported instances share a block device, not a general shared filesystem.",
          "text_sha256": "03f744012a65e53826af20afa668f4e7e57604b588f99f32b03031c170776f35",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b94d0491db1ee64ff5c34ebf153c157cd739be6cc407bd5bbb63c9694cb845e2",
          "asset_sha256": "516826adf50562626a931e89b4bddd0f4dbe682a64d2984ea2f97a1db32b68cf"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p20-andrew-exp-s02-c1-a1ade3f133d5",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Now suppose two Linux clients need the same report. They connect by N F S through their mount targets to one E F S directory tree. When one saves the report, another authorized client can read it as a shared file.",
          "text_sha256": "a1ade3f133d559ca47e63b81e281f422a4085504c6a40cf04adbf19c52bd9526",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "03dc0bbc3e5845cf0064316199983cb2c48a7cae2848e731534cb3b86b6b2250",
          "asset_sha256": "d1ac2cae61478a703f7766dc721d7977a77dfe0fc527f1ab8f36060457b89873"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p20-andrew-exp-s02-c2-4cc5756639ac",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Regional E F S stores data across zones; One Zone does not. Whichever you choose, the clients still need a network path and the right file permissions. This is not a native Windows S M B share.",
          "text_sha256": "4cc5756639ac76d839e5970ba300a3f74de476492dfe84e5a99b9b5b1cac87db",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b22372fed8b807562b4364255911db1a6d57aed938bda7d4cfe0810fb5c36bf3",
          "asset_sha256": "d1ac2cae61478a703f7766dc721d7977a77dfe0fc527f1ab8f36060457b89873"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p20-andrew-exp-s03-c1-55546841f1ca",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "When Windows clients need S M B, directory identity and Windows permissions, choose F S x for Windows File Server.",
          "text_sha256": "55546841f1ca83d272d89b476e0fbdde0140f3c0df8d3a6ed4f46f838dee6693",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b6332c3ed251c3cb6662f949b8c1ee527c4bc36aa93559fd79ac702e9ce49ce8",
          "asset_sha256": "34258d0c96e8494227fa11b57fe718f137748caef619356632a1f4b7dc4e758f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p20-andrew-exp-s03-c2-49b47721f1d2",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "For high-performance parallel processing with compatible clients, consider Lustre. The reason is the shared workload, not the Windows protocol.",
          "text_sha256": "49b47721f1d2763b76c1f90cd4198cb0113c435f8a2f38a5596e854e70e3b2ff",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "49b47721f1d2763b76c1f90cd4198cb0113c435f8a2f38a5596e854e70e3b2ff",
          "asset_sha256": "34258d0c96e8494227fa11b57fe718f137748caef619356632a1f4b7dc4e758f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p20-andrew-exp-s03-c3-b5eeb6b14bdd",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "on tap can fit supported combinations of file and block protocols such as N F S, S M B and eye scuzzy. Choose it when those interfaces match the client's actual access needs.",
          "text_sha256": "b5eeb6b14bdd99ac3b0d39b024524d008dc76b9b3c7bf6e1b2c4c5bb85033f2b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9090e7aaf2a50d2ab34e4b9904cd9e61c1e12775d447dc69bb93221b0c64ff08",
          "asset_sha256": "34258d0c96e8494227fa11b57fe718f137748caef619356632a1f4b7dc4e758f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m10p20-andrew-exp-s03-c4-94c2cb99a984",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "For an N F S workload that benefits from ZFS snapshots and clones, consider Open Z F S. A W S operates the file infrastructure, but the protocol, performance and recovery choices are still yours.",
          "text_sha256": "94c2cb99a98417949e7896b3cf23b7c4e3f51c18852d5d63d7028c2c07d29761",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ebeea030ac0fe0f6697da9fa57dff94e32968985c175965e8faeb2879d6c0681",
          "asset_sha256": "34258d0c96e8494227fa11b57fe718f137748caef619356632a1f4b7dc4e758f"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "11",
      "part": "01",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m11p01-andrew-expressive",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "7faccaf17c3f3610a4a5f865ef7c8f7aa13ba98856af7235f275c91e169ac915",
        "2": "880d48dbc3b1a2b8b61435ef70fae2aaebd7a7c426da0fc9e8192099b781ec19",
        "3": "5a9abb4d98fd7d173b903996f62132983b485a8e67e903e275c17913085f4aea",
        "4": "2ed475e1014a847c2ee832df79baf6ccd4f70376c5419725ac86e0ae8ed10fab"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m11p01-andrew-exp-s01-c1-f3ccca131dba",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Your app needs to join orders and customers and commit a payment. That combination fits relational S Q L, such as a suitable R D S engine or Aurora. Start with what the app asks the database to do.",
          "text_sha256": "f3ccca131dba79c8b7bdf2f797f9e06eaa84275c167d43c890188855b49582e4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "74bae639d9d08f1dfbaa815db1d32bd86889ea837627404d392ab89d7a50dd86",
          "asset_sha256": "7faccaf17c3f3610a4a5f865ef7c8f7aa13ba98856af7235f275c91e169ac915"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p01-andrew-exp-s01-c2-971e25ce0e73",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "If the app mainly retrieves an order by a known key, DynamoDB can fit. Design around the key and access pattern the application actually uses.",
          "text_sha256": "971e25ce0e734f732dfa1b78b4e654320a9a909483b01c4c04db10b186eb0353",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "971e25ce0e734f732dfa1b78b4e654320a9a909483b01c4c04db10b186eb0353",
          "asset_sha256": "7faccaf17c3f3610a4a5f865ef7c8f7aa13ba98856af7235f275c91e169ac915"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p01-andrew-exp-s01-c3-bfc405615e66",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Sensor readings are time-series data, so consider Timestream for InfluxDB. A W S no longer offers LiveAnalytics to new customers. If you instead retrieve nested records as documents, evaluate a document database such as DocumentDB.",
          "text_sha256": "bfc405615e6670609ee1e3ca49fa406c9a104d25ae6981ace0bdd941a1dbec1e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4ee8458036b517b470d59f39c13896ae637ca09c87f4a100e6b5d96c6098ed7c",
          "asset_sha256": "7faccaf17c3f3610a4a5f865ef7c8f7aa13ba98856af7235f275c91e169ac915"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p01-andrew-exp-s01-c4-ff908dcfc293",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "For a relevance-ranked product search, consider OpenSearch. If the problem is repeatedly reading the same hot value, a cache can serve it faster. That cache is not the authoritative order store in this design.",
          "text_sha256": "ff908dcfc293369bae15be71d59e0df240959925b0f033b9b90b679466cfc07f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ff908dcfc293369bae15be71d59e0df240959925b0f033b9b90b679466cfc07f",
          "asset_sha256": "7faccaf17c3f3610a4a5f865ef7c8f7aa13ba98856af7235f275c91e169ac915"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p01-andrew-exp-s02-c1-92f0d31ec325",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The client connects to the R D S D N S endpoint and engine port. The security group determines whether that path is allowed, before you get to database login.",
          "text_sha256": "92f0d31ec325c7aa9c175c511f895d0872fa88358d951e1ab6733c13265ad75a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "6700aa2a6716ab7dd6f33f7abf1ed1245554e36b8148edac662986856bb86bd1",
          "asset_sha256": "880d48dbc3b1a2b8b61435ef70fae2aaebd7a7c426da0fc9e8192099b781ec19"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p01-andrew-exp-s02-c2-ded6a836ec73",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Inside the managed instance, choose the engine and version, compute class, storage and parameter group. Adding disk capacity does not automatically tune a query.",
          "text_sha256": "ded6a836ec7317e57e06aa3d1da990187da13300865d7c03d364e0b9af9d19f7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ded6a836ec7317e57e06aa3d1da990187da13300865d7c03d364e0b9af9d19f7",
          "asset_sha256": "880d48dbc3b1a2b8b61435ef70fae2aaebd7a7c426da0fc9e8192099b781ec19"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p01-andrew-exp-s02-c3-9e20796a4623",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The DB subnet group supplies eligible subnets, normally across at least two Availability Zones. A Single-AZ instance is deployed in one zone at a time; Multi-AZ is a separate availability choice.",
          "text_sha256": "9e20796a46238179ceb6ad443be2ea51be960de9a548ee5f8eade92e4078ab49",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9e20796a46238179ceb6ad443be2ea51be960de9a548ee5f8eade92e4078ab49",
          "asset_sha256": "880d48dbc3b1a2b8b61435ef70fae2aaebd7a7c426da0fc9e8192099b781ec19"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p01-andrew-exp-s03-c1-e65428bc39cb",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "R D S handles jobs such as instance provisioning, patching, automated backups when configured, and monitoring. That takes away platform work, not responsibility for how the application uses the database.",
          "text_sha256": "e65428bc39cbd0a4485edcc4e6b9943005d19f765ddc251024b5d6da813be078",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "475594808b0677a9d4ea8341a7307444fa903b96bc0eb92e5324fb36c9735d1c",
          "asset_sha256": "5a9abb4d98fd7d173b903996f62132983b485a8e67e903e275c17913085f4aea"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p01-andrew-exp-s03-c2-7d240e1a28ce",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "You still design schemas and indexes, tune queries, set database permissions, and choose capacity. Check engine and version compatibility before moving the application.",
          "text_sha256": "7d240e1a28ce1392e31c6c45bae456a3df001e447003e20998670211f2d6c3d0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7d240e1a28ce1392e31c6c45bae456a3df001e447003e20998670211f2d6c3d0",
          "asset_sha256": "5a9abb4d98fd7d173b903996f62132983b485a8e67e903e275c17913085f4aea"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p01-andrew-exp-s03-c3-a9048c738a57",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The hundred-gibibyte disk can grow within the configured autoscaling maximum. It cannot shrink automatically. More disk will not fix the workload if the real cause is CPU pressure, too many connections or a slow query.",
          "text_sha256": "a9048c738a577b4ec882873b02d427a0abd56973e4d96b807e636517ec70a99d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a9048c738a577b4ec882873b02d427a0abd56973e4d96b807e636517ec70a99d",
          "asset_sha256": "5a9abb4d98fd7d173b903996f62132983b485a8e67e903e275c17913085f4aea"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p01-andrew-exp-s04-c1-dbe20c7acb1f",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Trace the orders function through private D N S and routing, then the security group for the engine port. The function's A W S role does not create that route. A failed connection is a reason to check the network first.",
          "text_sha256": "dbe20c7acb1fc9a697e423951453fec54243629d283fa20700505c6394f8358c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f254c882c416c09db5451dc0e8b51bc4eceb03e05a1d4a4ac0508ef75a15793a",
          "asset_sha256": "2ed475e1014a847c2ee832df79baf6ccd4f70376c5419725ac86e0ae8ed10fab"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p01-andrew-exp-s04-c2-02d46046454e",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Once the client can reach the endpoint, T L S protects the session and database login identifies the user. The database checks permissions for the operation separately.",
          "text_sha256": "02d46046454ed9b3581ed1096a761757c02341f98883e3662288944fb66ca5f5",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "aaabe2f19b580de58e6728f635bc7436b2ad042735f0591d106222b2751e2479",
          "asset_sha256": "2ed475e1014a847c2ee832df79baf6ccd4f70376c5419725ac86e0ae8ed10fab"
        },
        {
          "id": "m11p01-andrew-exp-s04-c3-7528dc330d1e",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "In this example, the application connects to PostgreSQL on port fifty-four thirty-two as the reader. An open port lets the connection start; only the right database grant lets that user select the order row.",
          "text_sha256": "7528dc330d1e66e6269646d421b3b30a68ed9c458018473e7a514452e8734401",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7528dc330d1e66e6269646d421b3b30a68ed9c458018473e7a514452e8734401",
          "asset_sha256": "2ed475e1014a847c2ee832df79baf6ccd4f70376c5419725ac86e0ae8ed10fab"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
